<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6930" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Căsĭlīnum</span></b> ,
		i, n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town in Campania</i>, <i>on the
				Vulturnus</i>, <i>near the ancient Capua.</i> In
			its place stands the present Capua, <i><span class="en">Liv. 22,
				15, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">23, 17,
				8</span></i> sq., and 19, 1 sq.; <i><span class="en">Cic. Att.
				16, 8, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Phil. 2, 40, 102</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C.
				3, 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5, 9, §
			70</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Căsĭlīnenses</span></b> ,
			ium, m., <i>the inhabitants
				of Casilinum</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Inv. 2, 57,
			171</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Căsĭlīnātes</span></b> ,
				ium, m., the same, <i><span class="en">Val. Max. 7,
				6, 2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Căsĭlīnus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of Casilinum</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">limina, i. e. Casilini portae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					12, 426</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
